<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lam Sơn uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1418–1427</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lam Son uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lam-son">Lam Sơn</a> uprising was the revolt led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>, which had occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> since 1407. Starting from Lam Sơn in Thanh Hóa, the rebels fought a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war and then besieged the Ming in Đông Quan. After the defeat of the Ming relief army at Chi Lăng in 1427 the Chinese withdrew, and Lê Lợi founded the Later Lê dynasty in 1428.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lam-son-uprising.jpg" alt="Lam Sơn uprising" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leeaan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Lam_S%C6%A1n_uprising_(en).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
